I now have a complete picture. Here are my findings.

## Build system
- Maven (single module). Root: `/home/daniel/sandbox/pom.xml`, wrapper `/home/daniel/sandbox/mvnw`.
- DTOs are NOT hand-written source. They are generated from `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/resources/openapi.yml` by the `openapi-generator-maven-plugin` (pom.xml line ~370, `<generateModels>true</generateModels>`) into `target/generated-sources/...`. So `OwnerFieldsDto` / `OwnerDto` are defined by the OpenAPI schema, not a `.java` file in `src`.
- Run tests: `/home/daniel/sandbox/mvnw test` (all), or a single class e.g. `/home/daniel/sandbox/mvnw test -Dtest=BusinessDaysTest` / `-Dtest=AcceptanceTest`. JaCoCo coverage check is bound (pom.xml ~309-340). The app is Spring PetClinic REST with OfficeFloor function-injection request handling (see `/home/daniel/sandbox/CLAUDE.md`, `/home/daniel/sandbox/AGENTS.md`).

## 1. Membership identifier + year segment
`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/AssignOwnerMembershipNumber.java`
```java
15  public void service(@Val Owner owner) {
16      int yy = owner.getRegistrationDate().getYear() % 100;
17      owner.setMembershipNumber(String.format("%s-M%02d", owner.getCustomerCode(), yy));
18  }
```
Format `<customerCode>-M<YY>` where `<YY>` is the last two digits of the (already business-day-adjusted) registration date year. The `membershipNumber` field/getter/setter live in the Owner model (`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/model/Owner.java`, field line 92, accessors lines 282-286). The response field is described in `openapi.yml` lines 2162-2167.

Orchestration order is defined in `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/resources/officefloor/rest/api/owners.POST.yml` (validate -> default -> roll -> ... -> assignMembershipNumber, lines 44-85).

## 2. Tenure calculation (elapsed years / 365-day window)
`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/model/Owner.java`
```java
419  private long getTenureDays() {
420      if (this.registrationDate == null) {
421          return 0;
422      }
423      return ChronoUnit.DAYS.between(this.registrationDate, LocalDate.now());
424  }
```
Consumed in `getMembershipPoints()` (same file), which awards points when tenure exceeds 365 days:
```java
378  public int getMembershipPoints() {
...
389      if (getTenureDays() > 365) {
390          points += 3;
391      }
392      return points;
393  }
```
`getMembershipLevel()` (lines 400-412) derives 1-4 from those points. Note: tenure is measured in whole days via `ChronoUnit.DAYS` (a 365-day window), not calendar years.

A separate whole-years computation exists in `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/util/AgeBand.java` line 25 (`Period.between(birthDate, asAt).getYears()`) — that is owner age band, not tenure, but it is the other year-derived value in the codebase.

## 3. Business-day adjustment of the registration date
Shared rule: `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/BusinessDays.java`
```java
35  static LocalDate rollForward(LocalDate date) {
36      while (!isBusinessDay(date)) {
37          date = date.plusDays(1);
38      }
39      return date;
40  }
42  private static boolean isBusinessDay(LocalDate date) {
43      DayOfWeek day = date.getDayOfWeek();
44      return day != DayOfWeek.SATURDAY && day != DayOfWeek.SUNDAY
45              && !PUBLIC_HOLIDAYS.contains(date);
46  }
```
Fixed holiday set at lines 20-25 (2026-01-01, 01-26, 04-25, 12-25, 12-28).

Applied to the registration date: `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/RollRegistrationDateToBusinessDay.java`
```java
18  public void service(@Val OwnerFieldsDto request) {
19      request.setRegistrationDate(BusinessDays.rollForward(request.getRegistrationDate()));
20  }
```
Related date-handling steps in the same package:
- `DefaultOwnerRegistrationDate.java` (lines 15-19): defaults a missing date to `LocalDate.now()`.
- `ValidateOwnerRegistrationDate.java` (lines 16-25): rejects a future date with `FutureRegistrationDateException`.
- Exception + handler: `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/escalation/FutureRegistrationDateException.java` and `FutureRegistrationDateExceptionHandler.java` (400 response).

Chain order (owners.POST.yml lines 44-55): validate -> default -> roll, so the rolled date is what tenure, daily-limit and the membership year segment all use.

## 4. DTOs / response objects (and fiscalYear)
- Response schema is the Owner schema in `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/resources/openapi.yml`:
  - `registrationDate` lines 2071-2076
  - `membershipNumber` lines 2162-2167
  - `membershipPoints` lines 2168-2175, `membershipLevel` lines 2176-2184
  - `locality`/`timezone`/`bulkSignupWarning` lines 2185-2199
- Generated Java DTOs from that schema: `OwnerFieldsDto` and `OwnerDto` (used in the function classes; produced under `target/generated-sources`, no `src` file). The Owner model that carries these values at runtime is `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/model/Owner.java`.
- IMPORTANT: There is currently NO `fiscalYear` field anywhere in main source or in `openapi.yml` — a grep for `fiscal` across `src/main` returns nothing. `fiscalYear` only appears in the test below, i.e. it is an expected-but-unimplemented feature.

## 5. Tests
- `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/test/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/BusinessDaysTest.java` — full unit coverage of the business-day roll (weekday unchanged, Sat/Sun roll, weekday holiday, Friday holiday, consecutive holidays, New Year), lines 12-50.
- `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/test/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/acceptance/AcceptanceTest.java` — the fiscal-year acceptance test:
```java
7   /** fiscal-year: Move date-derived values to a fiscal-year basis, where the fiscal year starts on 1 July. R... */
11  void coreReturnsFiscalYear() throws Exception {
12      int id = createOwnerOk(structuredOwner());
13      JsonNode n = fetchOwner(id);
14      assertTrue(n.get("fiscalYear").asText().matches("FY\\d{2}"));
15  }
```
This expects a `fiscalYear` response field matching `FY\d{2}`, with the fiscal year starting 1 July — not yet implemented in main code.
- `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/test/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/acceptance/AcceptanceBase.java` — black-box harness for `POST /api/owners` + `GET /api/owners/{id}`. Relevant helpers: `structuredOwner()` (136-142), `fetchOwner()` (200-204), `toBusinessDay()` replicating the roll (268-274), pinned `HOLIDAYS` set (240-242), region/timezone/postcode reference maps (228-237), and `sha256hex`/`shaHex`/`luhn` for derived-value checks (282-321).

No existing test directly asserts the tenure/membership-points 365-day threshold or the membership-number year segment beyond what the acceptance base enables; the fiscalYear test is the only year-basis test and it currently targets an unimplemented field.

